From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: regulator: core: runtime switch for s2idle state-mem

regulator.s2idle_state_mem (writable at runtime, default 1) turns off
every regulator-state-mem sleep vote in s2idle, so a no-floor s2idle test
can run without the PMIC LDO/BOB/SMPS low-power modes that 0523-0526 put
in the RPMh sleep set. Change it only while the system is awake.

Not for shipping.
---
--- a/drivers/regulator/core.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/core.c
@@ -562,6 +562,16 @@ static int regulator_mode_constrain(struct regulator_dev *rdev,
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * DEBUG: 0 skips every regulator-state-mem sleep vote in s2idle. Change it
+ * only while awake so suspend and resume see the same setting.
+ */
+#undef MODULE_PARAM_PREFIX
+#define MODULE_PARAM_PREFIX "regulator."
+static bool s2idle_state_mem = true;
+module_param(s2idle_state_mem, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(s2idle_state_mem, "Apply regulator-state-mem in s2idle (default: true)");
+
 static inline struct regulator_state *
 regulator_get_suspend_state(struct regulator_dev *rdev, suspend_state_t state)
 {
@@ -577,7 +587,7 @@ regulator_get_suspend_state(struct regulator_dev *rdev, suspend_state_t state)
 	 * has no PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE devicetree binding).
 	 */
 	case PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE:
-		if (!rdev->desc->s2idle_uses_state_mem)
+		if (!rdev->desc->s2idle_uses_state_mem || !READ_ONCE(s2idle_state_mem))
 			return NULL;
 		fallthrough;
 	case PM_SUSPEND_MEM:
